cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cognoscenti or its benchmark artifacts, please cite this software and the public benchmark report."
title: "Cognoscenti: A Benchmark for Trustworthy AI Memory"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Achiral AI"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24203849"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Achiral-AI/cognoscenti"
url: "https://achiral.ai/benchmarks/ai-memory-benchmark"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: "Cognoscenti is a benchmark for probabilistic, non-deterministic AI memory. It scores memory behavior along three axes of trustworthiness — calibration (does stated confidence mean anything), stability (does it agree with itself when repeated), and scope (does it respect the boundaries it's told) — through a deterministic, seeded stream-eval harness with an ACT-R reference, five stability tests, and token accounting for a learning-vs-static tokens-over-time hypothesis. No live run against a vendor or Achiral system has been published yet; the Measurement framework diagrams in the README are schematics of the method, not results."
keywords:
  - "AI memory benchmark"
  - "trustworthy AI memory"
  - "cognitive memory systems"
  - "emergent memory systems"
  - "ACT-R"
  - "agent memory"
  - "RAG"
